{"availability":"available","full":"paimonsoror/telltaledns","name":"telltaledns","description":"A small, fast DNS resolver and ad blocker that explains every answer. Per-device rules, encrypted DNS, and clustering across a Raspberry Pi and Kubernetes.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-03T00:48:48Z","updated":"2026-10-10T14:57:37Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://paimonsoror.github.io/telltaledns/","topics":["adblock","dns","dns-over-https","dns-over-quic","dns-over-tls","dns-resolver","homelab","kubernetes","mcp","rust","self-hosted"],"demo":"https://paimonsoror.github.io/telltaledns/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:25.922Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:25.922Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:25.922Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T15:06:25.922Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Every connection on your network starts with a DNS lookup. TelltaleDNS answers it in microseconds, filters it by your rules per device, and shows you exactly who asked, what they asked, and why it answered the way it did. It runs on a Raspberry Pi, in Kubernetes, or on both as one cluster that keeps answering even when parts of it fail.","A telltale is the strip of yarn sailors tie to a sail to see what the wind is really doing. DNS is your network's telltale: it reveals what every device is up to.","The dashboard on a demo network. Every device, name, and address in it is made up."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/paimonsoror/telltaledns/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"81b5c7ff681085baef9a18ce97564090839831f87a91c1899052d51a68d16d48","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:26.069Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:26.069Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Every connection on your network starts with a DNS lookup. TelltaleDNS answers it in microseconds, filters it b